{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings","id":1509929,"title":"Scion: Germany - Campaign Preparations and Musings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-27T23:46:19-07:00","id":1509929,"title":"Scion: Germany - Campaign Preparations and Musings","content":"Soon, I will start my very first Scion campaign, and I am very excited. The basic premise is this:<br /> <br /> - The campaign will primarily take place in Germany and adjacent lands, with Kassel serving as the &quot;home base&quot; of the band - although they will travel a lot.<br /> - The campaign will be <i>heavily</i> inspired by my research on German folklore and folk tales, and I will always try to work local legends into the story.<br /> - The Scions will start at the Origin level. At some point they will rise up to the Hero level. Whether they want to rise to Demigod or further level will be up to them.<br /> <br /> Thus, to prepare for the campaign and in order to ruminate on campaign developments, I wanted to start a thread where I discuss aspects of the campaign in detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's start by about the Pantheons involved.<br /> <br /> Germany is sort-of border territory between the \u00c6sir, the Thenoi, and the Bogovi. The \u00c6sir are the strongest in the northwest, the Thenoi in the south and west, and the Bogovi in the east.<br /> <br /> The Thenoi, just like Christianity, came with the Roman Empire, and the ruling aristocracy often had a strong affinity with the Thenoi.<br /> <br /> The \u00c6sir got a huge boost thanks to the 19th century Nationalist Romantic revival. A lot of folklorists (including Jacob Grimm) saw hints and traces of Nordic mythology everywhere, whether valid or not - and others, including the Nazis, followed in their footsteps. Norse/Germanic mythology was often seen in contrast to the &quot;foreign&quot; Christian or Roman influences.<br /> <br /> Slavic mythology and beliefs were actively suppressed in German lands for a long time - there were several crusades in the early Middle Ages as Christianity tried to stamp out these beliefs. In The World, such attempts were obviously not as successful as in ours - but nevertheless, Western Slavic people were often forcefully assimilated into the German mainstream, barring some minorities such as the Sorbian people. This may have caused some resentment against other faiths. Nevertheless, old Slavic traces are everywhere in the Eastern parts of Germany, if you know where to look.<br /> <br /> During the Soviet Occupation of Eastern Germany, worshipers of the Bogovi saw something of a resurgence. Officially, the East German government discouraged all religions, but Christianity was more suspect to the state authorities than Slavic religious beliefs - especially since many Red Army members were also worshiping the Bogovi (and had an easier time practicing their beliefs than in the Homeland, where state security was watching more closely).<br /> <br /> <br /> There are also lots of remnants of old Celtic settlements and beliefs, but pretty much all the evidence is archaeological. Nevertheless, if the band delves into old Celtic fortresses and barrow-mounds - and they likely will, at some point - I need to figure out how to model their religious associations. Any suggestions? Variants of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann or the Nemetondevos, perhaps?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T00:48:26-07:00","id":1509931,"title":"","content":"My thoughts, as small Polish fan of <b>Scion</b> and author of Bogovi fan take <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1. What is your take on Myths Dials? Are 'Gods in Hiding' - or are they like in vanilla setting 'In open, but distant'? ( see <b>Scion Companion - Mysteries of the World</b> for more info on subject. )<br /> 2. As German ( as well Polish ) Celts were much more related to French ones than English - I would much more spring the Germany with last vistages of Nemetondevos than Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann. ( Nemetondevos are also desrbied in <b>Mysteries of the World</b>\u200b <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) From <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celts\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia on Celts</a> -<br /> <br /> <br /> <img width=\"505\" height=\"546\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8SQ0mXL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8SQ0mXL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8SQ0mXL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T01:29:05-07:00","id":1509934,"title":"","content":"Frankly, any continental Celtic myth would have to be a reconstruction. Both the 1st edition and the second use bizarre reconstructions of Irish myth. The first used Yeats' Celtic Hinduism the second tried to capture the medieval Clerical take on the Irish gods. The second was arguably more authentic but the first was much more fun and highly playable.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is go with playable. Make up a small pantheon based on the broad themes of Celtic myth as you see it. Remember, the Ancient Celts tend to give their students psychological whiplash. They are the pluperfect example of the phase &quot;Savages are cool, until they're savage.&quot; Although we don't get the jokes of the Ancient Celts (we do &quot;get&quot; Roman jokes even when they creep us out) we largely get their sense of humor. Then they do things we find unspeakably alien. Use that pattern. Alternatively charm and alienate they players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-28-2023, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T02:14:40-07:00","id":1509936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings?p=1509931#post1509931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts, as small Polish fan of <b>Scion</b> and author of Bogovi fan take <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1. What is your take on Myths Dials? Are 'Gods in Hiding' - or are they like in vanilla setting 'In open, but distant'? ( see <b>Scion Companion - Mysteries of the World</b> for more info on subject. )</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go with the &quot;open, but distant&quot; default. Pretty much everyone knows about the existence of the Gods and their worship, but it is largely possible to live a life without their direct interference if someone chooses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. As German ( as well Polish ) Celts were much more related to French ones than English - I would much more spring the Germany with last vistages of Nemetondevos than Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann. ( Nemetondevos are also desrbied in <b>Mysteries of the World</b>\u200b <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) From <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celts\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia on Celts</a> -<br /> <br /> <br /> <img width=\"505\" height=\"546\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8SQ0mXL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8SQ0mXL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8SQ0mXL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>After searching the forums, I came across <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos Revised</a>, a free community supplement. I think I'll largely use that for my campaign.<br /> <br /> By the way, can anyone recommend any other Storypath Nexus supplements that would be very useful for my campaign premise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings?p=1509934#post1509934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, any continental Celtic myth would have to be a reconstruction. Both the 1st edition and the second use bizarre reconstructions of Irish myth. The first used Yeats' Celtic Hinduism the second tried to capture the medieval Celrical take on the Irish gods. The second was arguably more authentic but the first was much more fun and highly playable.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is go with playable. Make up a small pantheon based on the broad themes of Celtic myth as you see it. Remember, the Ancient Celts tend to give their students psychological whiplash. They are the pluperfect example of the phase &quot;Savages are cool, until they're savage.&quot; Although we don't get the jokes of the Ancient Celts (we do &quot;get&quot; Roman jokes even when they creep us out) we largely get their sense of humor. Then they do things we find unspeakably alien. Use that pattern. Alternatively charm and alienate they players.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure yet whether any of my players will pick a Scion from the Nemetondevos. I've told them which four Pantheons have the most influence in the region, but I am leaving it open to them which God they pick as their parent - and I am not restricting them to those four, either.<br /> <br /> But there are Celtic traces all over Germany (many of which are associated with local legends), and thus I want to start figuring out what to do with them early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T12:06:23-07:00","id":1509975,"title":"","content":"I'd also think about what pantheons immigrants and refugees coming to Germany bring with them. Based on some very quick internet research, it looks like a lot of immigrants come from Eastern Europe, which would reinforce the importance of the Bogovoi. It also looks like there's a lot of migration from the Middle East, which might bring with it small groups of worshipers of the Annuna of Mesopotamia and the Ilhm of Canaan (included in the forthcoming God), possibly even the Netjer of Egypt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T12:21:44-07:00","id":1509981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings?p=1509936#post1509936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After searching the forums, I came across <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos Revised</a>, a free community supplement. I think I'll largely use that for my campaign.<br /> <br /> By the way, can anyone recommend any other Storypath Nexus supplements that would be very useful for my campaign premise?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's what you're looking for, but there is a take on the Theosophical Pantheon (the Ascended Masters), which (as the supplement notes) helped lay the foundation for the New Age movement. So, if you're open to a modern pantheon, they would likely have some presence in Germany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T13:16:07-07:00","id":1509984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muskrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings?p=1509975#post1509975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also think about what pantheons immigrants and refugees coming to Germany bring with them. Based on some very quick internet research, it looks like a lot of immigrants come from Eastern Europe, which would reinforce the importance of the Bogovoi. It also looks like there's a lot of migration from the Middle East, which might bring with it small groups of worshipers of the Annuna of Mesopotamia and the Ilhm of Canaan (included in the forthcoming God), possibly even the Netjer of Egypt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's easy to justify arrival of Pantheons and their worshipers and Scions from all over the world. However, my primary focus is on tying in old German folk tales, and the four &quot;old, established&quot; Pantheons work best for that.<br /> <br /> That being said, Netjer influence dates back to at least the 19th century - while it might not have been as extreme as in the British Empire, Germany too had its bouts of Egyptomania. I once visited the <a href=\"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammer_(N%C3%BCrnberg)\" target=\"_blank\">former estate of an industrialist in Nuremberg</a>, and they a genuine fake Egyptian obelisk:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Hammer_14.jpg/450px-Hammer_14.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T14:00:28-07:00","id":1509990,"title":"","content":"I often equate Muslim population with Netjer Pantheon, as Egypt as one of first big 'wins' of Muslims, de fact stating their legacy as detentes of Egypts ancient culture. ( Which historically is more like Muslims started as rebelled provinces of Byzantine Empire, but it's digression. ) With Pantheons of Ancient Persia ( Yazata, if I recall? ) and Ancient Mezopotamia ( Annuna ) being almost wiped out, Muslims sustaining Netjer traditions in modern World is good take. With Netjer being so much about Law and Tradition it also nicely works with many Muslim dogmas. ( See my fan take on <b>HtV</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1496082-conspiracies-as-evil-antagonists-factions?p=1496096#post1496096\">Ascending Ones as sustaing Netjer dogmas in modern World</a>. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T23:07:23-07:00","id":1510040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings?p=1509990#post1509990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often equate Muslim population with Netjer Pantheon, as Egypt as one of first big 'wins' of Muslims, de fact stating their legacy as detentes of Egypts ancient culture. ( Which historically is more like Muslims started as rebelled provinces of Byzantine Empire, but it's digression. ) With Pantheons of Ancient Persia ( Yazata, if I recall? ) and Ancient Mezopotamia ( Annuna ) being almost wiped out, Muslims sustaining Netjer traditions in modern World is good take. With Netjer being so much about Law and Tradition it also nicely works with many Muslim dogmas. ( See my fan take on <b>HtV</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1496082-conspiracies-as-evil-antagonists-factions?p=1496096#post1496096\">Ascending Ones as sustaing Netjer dogmas in modern World</a>. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Muslim immigrants to Germany are from Turkey, and that's a very distinct cultural heritage from the Arab world (including Egypt). In fact, modern Turkey was founded as an explicit rejection of any kind of pan-Arabism, and an embrace of a distinct Turkish identity (including rejecting cultural and linguistic minorities within the borders of Turkey).<br /> <br /> If I were to use existing Pantheons for local worshipers, I'd look at the Thenoi, Yazata, and even the Tengri rather than the Netjer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T03:14:34-07:00","id":1510180,"title":"","content":"So, one of the first adventures I am planning is a treasure hunt of sorts, which is <i>traditional</i> in German folk tales.<br /> <br /> None of the PCs are really affluent, so this should be tempting for at least some of them. And if they keep their wits about them and succeed, they will end up with a classical chest full of gold coins.<br /> <br /> However, then their troubles might only start. In their part of Germany, the law states clearly that any such found treasures from previous centuries belong to the state. Thus, they will have to figure out how to actually spend it on things they want. If they only use it in the Mythic Underground, this might work out, although not all supernatural citizens are interested in cash.<br /> <br /> But if they want to spend it on mundane things, then they would first have to find a &quot;trustworthy&quot; black market dealer who is willing to exchange their gold into unmarked bills - or cryptocurrency, depending. And if they flout their new wealth, the authorities might become suspicious on just where they suddenly got all this money - doubly so if any electronic funds were involved.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for ideas on how I can handle this in the game, particularly if it is done in an amusing (for me) or embarrassing (for the player character characters) manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T11:33:52-07:00","id":1510714,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any good ideas for rival treasure hunters (that would fit in at the Origin level)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T13:32:18-07:00","id":1510717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1509929-scion-germany-campaign-preparations-and-musings?p=1510714#post1510714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any good ideas for rival treasure hunters (that would fit in at the Origin level)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hiers of Dragons. Dragons love trusears. \ud83d\udc09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T15:12:41-07:00","id":1510724,"title":"","content":"The creatures in the fairy tale &quot;Snow White and Rose Red&quot; were obsessed with treasure. The English language translations the creature is called a Dwarf or a Gnome, I assume you'd know the correct terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T08:19:56-07:00","id":1510794,"title":"","content":"Depending on how vile you want the rival treasure hunters to be, you could make them Nazi occultists. In the real world, Himmler wanted to find things like the Holy Grail and Thor's hammer. This only works if you're looking for outright villains, as opposed to just rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}